<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CBR009 Replacement Structures Summary, ported from legacy's JasperServer report
  (cbr-legacy jasper-server .../CBR009_ReplacementStructureSummary.rpt_jrxml), its layout kept but
  for three faults:
  - Legacy printed "REPLACEMENT YEAR / REPLACEMENT FOR" only where a year started, so a page it ran
    onto showed column headings under no year; it is now on every page, marked "(continued)".
  - Every value was one fixed line, so a long Structure #, Road Name, Crossing Name or Primary User
    Name was cut off; each value now wraps, and the row's column lines grow with it - but a number,
    which shrinks to fit its column instead.
  - The column headed "Year Superstructure Fabricated" printed ORIGINAL_REPLACEMENT_DATE, the
    structure's End of Design Life, under a stray "End of Design Life" label above the table; the
    column is now headed so, and the stray label is gone.
  As in the other reports, the port fills from rows rather than SQL - legacy called
  CBR_RPLCMNT_STRUCTURE_RPT with a WHERE clause built as a string - every field already formatted
  as legacy's patterns printed it, and each year's totals computed with the rows (TOTAL_COST,
  TOTAL_COUNT). SECTION_KEY is the district and management area a page is for, YEAR_KEY the year
  and section within it. The ministry line (the CBR_HEADER subreport) is P_MINISTRY, the logo
  P_LOGO, and Date Printed P_DATE_PRINTED, in Pacific time.
-->
